// F16.log, F32.log, and F64.log are correctly rounded: ln(x) / ln(base) rounded once to nearest-even, checked
// against mpmath for random positive finite pairs, hard cases (near 1, exact powers such as log(1000, 10) = 3,
// subnormals, the ends of the range, x = base), and every pair within 8 ulps of 1. Near 1 the true quotient can sit
// extremely close to a midpoint: log(1 - 2^-52, 1 + 2^-50) is within 2^-154 of one, past F64.log's F128 tier, so it
// takes the F128Big tier. They used to round three times (each logarithm, then the quotient, in the type itself).

